#html.elem("p", attrs: (style: "color: var(--calepin-color-link); font-size: 2em; font-weight: bold;"))[Tables of contents]

Bookly defines several commands to create tables of contents. Their titles are translated according to the `lang` argument of `#bookly.with`.

= Book outlines

- `#tableofcontents`: table of contents
- `#listoffigures`: list of figures
- `#listoftables`: list of tables

```typ
#show: main-matter

#tableofcontents
#listoffigures
#listoftables
```

= Mini table of contents

A mini table of contents listing the sections of the current chapter is generated by the `#minitoc` command. Its style is defined by the current theme.

```typ
= First chapter

#minitoc

== First section
```

#calepin.elements.callout[
  `#minitoc` is a wrapper of the `suboutline` function provided by the #link("https://typst.app/universe/package/suboutline")[`suboutline`] package. When you use the `#chapter` function with `toc: true` (the default), the mini table of contents is inserted automatically (see #link("parts-chapters.html#chapters")[Chapters]).
]
